### Analysis and Audit Summary

#### 1. Audit of `Lasers.js` and Test Status
An exhaustive disassembly and audit of `Lasers.class` (`javap -p -c -cp /tmp/ra1jar Lasers`) was conducted against [`Lasers.js`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/Lasers.js) and [`Lasers.test.js`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/Lasers.test.js):
- **Screen Projection (`xs`, `ys`)**: Tested for boundary clamping (`j < 10`), 32-bit integer arithmetic wrapping with `Math.imul` and `idiv`, and focus point offsets (`Medium.focus_point`).
- **Rotation (`rot`)**: Verified float32 precision for `SinCos.getsin`/`getcos` trigonometric operations (`fr()` wrapping on intermediate float binary operations) and int32 coordinate truncations.
- **3D Transform & Painter's Algorithm (`dt`, `d`)**: Verified vertex coordinate jittering and polygon rendering without depth buffers or reordering.
- **§2 Compound Assignment Classification**:
  - `dt()` lines 146–151 (bytecode offsets 70–101, 102–133, 134–166): `iaload; i2d; ...; dadd; d2i; iastore` — accumulator widened to double before addition with one truncation at the end (**Case A**). Implemented as `ai[n] = trunc(ai[n] + (...))`.

#### 2. Root Cause of Failures in `Lasers.fail.txt`
The test log [`Lasers.fail.txt`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/decompilation/logs/Lasers.fail.txt) was produced when the test harness ran the entire suite `cd /home/evan/resources/ra1/port && node --test`.
- All 6 tests for [`Lasers.js`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/Lasers.js) in [`Lasers.test.js`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/Lasers.test.js) passed completely.
- The 4 failures in that log came from [`userCraft.test.js`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/userCraft.test.js) due to compound-assignment classifications and lift calculation bugs in `userCraft.js`.
- [`Lasers.js`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/Lasers.js) is 100% compliant with the JVM bytecode and TRANSPILE_SPEC.

